Course content licence
======================

Everything under `data/` (lexicon entries, sentences, microstories, and the
compiled courses in `data/dist/`) is licensed under

    Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International
    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/

CC BY-SA is chosen deliberately: it is compatible with Wiktionary, which is the
upstream source for morphological facts (gender, plural, conjugation) once the
full pipeline runs. If the content were licensed more permissively, Wiktionary
data could not be mixed in.

Upstream sources and their licences
-----------------------------------

| Source                     | Licence          | Used for                          |
|----------------------------|------------------|-----------------------------------|
| OpenSubtitles frequency     | CC BY-SA 4.0     | Spoken-German word frequency      |
| (hermitdave/FrequencyWords) |                  | `data/sources/de_50k.txt`         |
| Leipzig Corpora Collection  | CC BY 4.0        | Written-German frequency (opt-in) |
| Wiktionary via kaikki.org   | CC BY-SA 4.0 +   | Gender, plural, conjugation       |
| (wiktextract)               | GFDL             |                                   |
| Tatoeba                     | CC BY 2.0 FR     | Example sentences (opt-in)        |

Attribution for the frequency data currently shipped:

    Hermit Dave, FrequencyWords (2018), derived from the OpenSubtitles corpus.
    https://github.com/hermitdave/FrequencyWords — CC BY-SA 4.0

The hand-authored lexicon glosses, example sentences and microstories in
`data/de/` are original work by the project contributors, released under the
same CC BY-SA 4.0 licence.
